#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: kr-summon-anonymous-given
backends: [int, js, jvm, v2]
---

# `summon` over an ANONYMOUS `given`

Executable record of BUGS.md `interp-summon-over-an-anonymous-given`, which had no gate.

The named form — `given intCombiner: Combiner[Int] with` — has always worked. The gap is the
ANONYMOUS spelling, which is the idiomatic Scala 3 one and the one every typeclass module in
`std/` uses. Both spellings are in the case, so a fix that only reaches one of them cannot go
green: the named line proves the machinery is present, the anonymous line is the defect.

```scalascript
trait Combiner[A]:
  def combine(a: A, b: A): A

given namedCombiner: Combiner[String] with
  def combine(a: String, b: String): String = a + b

given Combiner[Int] with
  def combine(a: Int, b: Int): Int = a + b

def main(): Unit =
  println(summon[Combiner[String]].combine("a", "b"))
  println(summon[Combiner[Int]].combine(2, 3))
  val c = summon[Combiner[Int]]
  println(c.combine(2, 3))

main()
```
